{
 "turns": [
  {
   "idx": 0,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Hi, I'm Dr.",
   "start": 0.11,
   "end": 1.37
  },
  {
   "idx": 1,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Mailingchoo.",
   "start": 1.65,
   "end": 2.13
  },
  {
   "idx": 2,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Come on in, have a seat. Can you tell me your full name and date of birth? Adise Arkhafer,",
   "start": 2.59,
   "end": 7.91
  },
  {
   "idx": 3,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "February 14, 2005.",
   "start": 8.49,
   "end": 10.33
  },
  {
   "idx": 4,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Valentine's baby.",
   "start": 11.57,
   "end": 12.19
  },
  {
   "idx": 5,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Okay, Adise, what brings you in?",
   "start": 12.75,
   "end": 14.43
  },
  {
   "idx": 6,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "My acne. I've had it since, like, 18, but the last",
   "start": 15.17,
   "end": 18.19
  },
  {
   "idx": 7,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "six months it's gotten so much worse.",
   "start": 18.19,
   "end": 20.03
  },
  {
   "idx": 8,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "It's on my face and some on my upper back. What have you tried so far? I used a benzoyl peroxide wash, the ten percent one, for about a month, but I stopped it",
   "start": 20.61,
   "end": 31.0
  },
  {
   "idx": 9,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "in the summer because it bleached all my towels and my pillowcases.",
   "start": 31.0,
   "end": 34.14
  },
  {
   "idx": 10,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "That's really common. Did it help at all while you were using it? A little, I guess, not enough.",
   "start": 35.0,
   "end": 39.96
  },
  {
   "idx": 11,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any medicines or supplements you take? I'm on the birth control pill, the norgestimate one, once a day,",
   "start": 40.64,
   "end": 46.52
  },
  {
   "idx": 12,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "and vitamin D3, two thousand units a day.",
   "start": 47.1,
   "end": 49.8
  },
  {
   "idx": 13,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any allergies to medications? Amoxicillin, I got hives all over when I was a kid.",
   "start": 50.24,
   "end": 55.74
  },
  {
   "idx": 14,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay,",
   "start": 56.64,
   "end": 56.7
  },
  {
   "idx": 15,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "are your periods regular? Yes, pretty regular, on the pill anyway. Any extra hair growth on your chin or chest?",
   "start": 57.18,
   "end": 64.23
  },
  {
   "idx": 16,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No.",
   "start": 64.91,
   "end": 65.19
  },
  {
   "idx": 17,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And does the acne leave scars or dark spots?",
   "start": 66.24,
   "end": 68.78
  },
  {
   "idx": 18,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Dark spots, yeah, I don't think scars. Let me take a look. On your forehead, cheeks and jawline you've got lots",
   "start": 69.76,
   "end": 76.12
  },
  {
   "idx": 19,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "of open and closed cometones. so blackheads and whiteheads, about 15 red -inflamed bumps, and maybe 6 pustules. There are a few tender 4mm nodules along the jawline, no large cysts. You have some flat dark brown spots on both cheeks, that's post -inflammatory hyperpigmentation. I don't see any scarring.",
   "start": 76.12,
   "end": 94.28
  },
  {
   "idx": 20,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "On the upper back, scattered red papules, maybe 10 or so. So is it bad?",
   "start": 94.7,
   "end": 99.4
  },
  {
   "idx": 21,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I'd call this moderate acne vulgaris, with some dark spots from old breakouts. The good news is it's very treatable. I'd like to start two things. First, a Dapalene 0 .1 % gel, a pea -sized amount to your whole face at night. Start every other night for the first two weeks, because it can make your skin dry and a little peely.",
   "start": 100.2,
   "end": 120.76
  },
  {
   "idx": 22,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay. Second, doxycycline 100 milligrams twice a",
   "start": 121.18,
   "end": 125.98
  },
  {
   "idx": 23,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "day for three months. Take it with food and a full glass of water, and stay upright for 30 minutes after, so it doesn't irritate your esophagus. Keep it two hours away from dairy, calcium, or iron.",
   "start": 125.98,
   "end": 138.2
  },
  {
   "idx": 24,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Got it. Is it okay with my birth control? Yes, it doesn't make your pill less effective. Now,",
   "start": 138.8,
   "end": 145.05
  },
  {
   "idx": 25,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "an important question.",
   "start": 145.39,
   "end": 146.27
  },
  {
   "idx": 26,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Is there any chance you could be pregnant right now? No, my last period was two weeks ago. But, um, if I did get pregnant, could I keep taking these?",
   "start": 146.89,
   "end": 155.19
  },
  {
   "idx": 27,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "No, and that's a really good question. Doxycycline can affect a baby's teeth and bones, and we don't use adaptiline in pregnancy either. So if you ever think you might be pregnant, stop both and call us.",
   "start": 155.97,
   "end": 168.45
  },
  {
   "idx": 28,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay, that makes sense.",
   "start": 169.07,
   "end": 170.29
  },
  {
   "idx": 29,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "The other big thing with doxycycline is sun sensitivity. You can burn really fast on it. So sunscreen, SPF 30 or higher every morning, and a hat if you're out a lot. The adaptiline makes you more sun sensitive too.",
   "start": 171.27,
   "end": 185.53
  },
  {
   "idx": 30,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I walk across campus all day at Lakeshore State, so I'll be careful. Good. I'd also like you to go back to benzoyl peroxide, but the gentler four percent wash,",
   "start": 186.07,
   "end": 195.75
  },
  {
   "idx": 31,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "once in the morning.",
   "start": 196.19,
   "end": 197.03
  },
  {
   "idx": 32,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "It keeps bacteria from getting resistant to the antibiotic. Use white towels and you won't care about the bleaching. Ah, okay. My roommate Priya was on a cutane last year and it totally cleared her up. Should I just do that?",
   "start": 197.67,
   "end": 210.75
  },
  {
   "idx": 33,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That's a stronger medicine we save for severe or scarring acne. me. Yours isn't there, so let's see how this does first. Which pharmacy do you use?",
   "start": 211.17,
   "end": 219.89
  },
  {
   "idx": 34,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "The one on 4120 Belmont Avenue. Okay, I'll send both there, and a call back number. 555 -0118. Perfect.",
   "start": 220.63,
   "end": 231.27
  },
  {
   "idx": 35,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "It takes 8 to 12 weeks to see the full effect, so hang in there. Let's see you back in 3 months.",
   "start": 231.87,
   "end": 237.13
  },
  {
   "idx": 36,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "If you get a really bad sunburn,",
   "start": 237.71,
   "end": 239.31
  },
  {
   "idx": 37,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "bad stomach upset, or headaches with vision changes on the doxycycline, stop it and call us. We'll do, thank you so much.",
   "start": 239.73,
   "end": 247.65
  }
 ],
